{{- /*
Meson options for the libspice-server build. Included by images/spice-server/werf.inc.yaml.

The library is built here rather than taken from pm because the behaviour we need
to change is not exposed at all: the gstreamer encoder hardcodes which elements
it asks for, and the thresholds of the video-area detector are compile-time
constants in server/video-stream.h. Both are patch territory, see
patches/README.md.

The layout is pinned for the same reason libvirt pins it: meson's own defaults
(prefix=/usr/local, libdir=lib) would put the library where neither the qemu
build nor virt-launcher looks for it.

gstreamer is on, at version 1.0. The encoder needs four pkg-config modules
(gstreamer-1.0, -base-1.0, -app-1.0, -video-1.0), all of which pm provides in
gstreamer-devel alongside the gst-plugins-base and gst-plugins-good packages.
Without them the server is limited to its built-in MJPEG encoder for streamed areas,
which compresses every frame on its own; vp8 is the reason for the whole exercise.

Only vp8 and vp9 are available through it. h264 would need x264enc, which spice
asks for by name and which lives in gst-plugins-ugly under the GPL; the pm packages
carry neither that plugin set nor its encoder.

opus is enabled: without it the playback channel stays at
SPICE_AUDIO_DATA_MODE_RAW (server/sound.cpp), which is audible but sends the guest
audio uncompressed, and the fallback to RAW remains in place anyway for clients
that cannot decode opus.

lz4 is on, it is the image compression the console actually benefits from, and
pm carries lz4 1.10.0 against the required 1.7.3.

smartcard is disabled: libcacard is not in pm and the module does not pass
smartcards through. sasl is off because the console is authenticated at the API
layer, long before a client reaches this socket. manual and tests build nothing
that ships.

generate-code is not set here on purpose: spice already selects `server` for the
spice-common subproject, so the client-side marshallers are not generated.
*/ -}}
--prefix=/usr \
-Dlibdir=/usr/lib64 \
-Dgstreamer=1.0 \
-Dopus=enabled \
-Dsmartcard=disabled \
-Dsasl=false \
-Dlz4=true \
-Dtests=false \
-Dmanual=false \
-Dinstrumentation=no
